nd full-record native test and actual closed reaper verify89 ownership ranges with unchanged rendered geometry. The separate README count correction preserves the honest historical typo; actualRESULT had the right counts. Two-path patch remains external/prepared at this checkpoint; no browser PASS is inferred.\n\nThe initial54 source gate ran serially because a four-core browser was active. Once the browser ended, the remaining serial timing estimate exceeded the cost of a full standard four-worker gate. Root stopped ONLY mainBash2654041, allowed its current child test to finish naturally, verified all non-root owned processes nonlive, then delivered TERM and CONT only to the stopped parent. Actual Linux signal exit is-15, conventionally143; this is an honest owner interruption/NQ, not a product failure or PASS. All source/tree/index/ref/config/ticket/own/foreign guards remained exact before and after. Original serial logs/timings/reaper are archived; unchanged reaper completion remains unknown. The old recovered-PASS preparation was never executed and cannot accept this actual signal exit.\n\nA new ordinary four-core native1105 source gate has been launched in an explicitly detached controller2671988, CHECK_JOBS4, CPUs0,1,3,4,nice19, using the same approved3545 staged source and funded single1.557GB transient scratch. Its immutable preparation and launchOWNER are saved. EVERY active actual four-core binding/log/TMP/timing/reaper/result remains excluded, even if it completes while this archive publishes. Actual source gate, native checkpoint[3746,54], phone, CI and normal dev merge must be observed separately.\n\nNamed8b import and two-owner/two-lap generated settlement preparation are saved, including exact immutable public commit/tree/object/mode/hash metadata. The76 encoded public object bodies are deliberately omitted, not silently missing: EXPLICIT-PUBLIC-IMPORT-PAYLOAD-OMISSIONS.json names every omitted path,size,hash and exact reconstruction condition. Regene